        "bhavartha": "The singer owns that he has none of the usual ways of devotion: no yoga, no japa, not even worship. All he has is his bow, and he stays bowed before Śambhu always, at every moment. Burning again and again in the flood of sorrow that old age and birth bring, he asks the Lord to protect him in his distress."
